# Binary irreducibility of the scalar-sensitive point-parabolic flags

All four literal constituents are irreducible among arbitrary additive
subgroups, and noncentral when |F| = 2^n with n > 1. Their orders are 2^n
for the scalar factors and 2^(2*n) for the planes. The actual SL₂ section
and the alternating-form intertwiner identify both plane restrictions
with the natural module, retaining the full GL₂ actions and scalar characters.

The source point, its literal quotient, and every marked upper/lower copy
carry these actions through the genuine surjective projection from L₁.
The prior MarkedLayers premises stay explicit. Radical minimality and the
final chief-factor assembly are separate obligations. No distinction of
binary isomorphism types between the two scalar characters is asserted.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, G.2.1 and G.2.5(6–8), printed pp.332,335–336.
-/
